<title>GERMANY: Rheinmetall sees 1997 earnings boost.</title>
<headline>Rheinmetall sees 1997 earnings boost.</headline>
<dateline>DUESSELDORF, Germany 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German defense and engineering group Rheinmetall AG said on Monday that recent acquisitions would boost both turnover and profits in 1997 after an earnings recovery this year.</p>
<p>Chief executive Hans Brauner told a news conference that taking management control of electronics firm STN Atlas and the buy-out of Richard Hirschmann &amp; Co would bring a &quot;quantum leap&quot; in the company's next business year.  </p>
<p>Rheinmetall sees 1997 earnings boost</p>
<p>He said the acquisitions would boost turnover in 1997 to 5.5 billion marks and pre-tax profits would rise to 130 million marks.</p>
<p>Sales in 1996 were expected to rise 4.8 percent to 3.6 billion marks and net profit would be in double-digit millions after 2.6 million marks the year before.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 2609750</p>
